WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.370
The buzz about "The Batman" is full of ups
and downs.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:06.870
On the one hand, it's the darkest, most frightening
vision of the Dark Knight yet.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:10.190
On the other, that makes it easy to wonder
why this Batman's so bulletproof.

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.630
These are the best and worst things about
"The Batman."

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.870
"I don't care what happens to me."

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.680
"It's only gonna get worse for you."

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.300
Batman is known for his combat prowess.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.070
In most iterations of the character, he's
traveled the world and learned countless methods

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.720
of hand-to-hand combat and all forms of martial
arts.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.790
In "The Batman," he's seemingly acquired most
of his talent from Alfred, a man who, this

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.789
time around, we learn little about.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:35.970
Regardless, Batman doesn't disappoint as he
dismantles the criminal element piece by piece

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.090
using almost nothing but his fists.

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:41.660
The opening sequence, where we see the Dark
Knight approach a violent street gang, is

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.530
the first introduction we have to the hero's
capabilities on the ground.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:48.900
The cocky leader taunts and assaults a costumed
man he clearly doesn't understand and quickly

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.480
learns a lesson the hard way.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.520
Batman's attack is swift and merciless.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.250
If the sounds of brutality are any indication,
this thug will likely be eating through a

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.530
straw for a while.

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:01.100
At the other end of the film, when the Riddler
enacts his plan to flood Gotham, we once again

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.210
witness Batman's talent for dishing out pain
as he takes on several of Riddler's followers

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.469
— all of whom are armed to the teeth.

00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:11.200
Batman's armor deflects bullets while he expertly
moves from person to person, putting each

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.229
out of commission.

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:16.130
The fight choreography is tight and exciting
to watch throughout the film.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.950
Make no mistake, the Batman costume looks
great, and Robert Pattinson wears the new

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:20.950
Batsuit well.

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:24.969
Beyond aesthetics, however, there's an unexplained
durability to the suit that becomes rather

00:01:24.969 --> 00:01:26.499
conspicuous in the movie.

00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:29.369
Sure, Batman is going to develop an armor
that can withstand some gunfire.

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:30.369
That's a given.

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:33.409
But how about armor that can withstand a barrage
of gunfire?

00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:37.060
Throughout the film, Batman is shot directly
countless times and is typically no worse

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.189
for wear.

00:01:38.189 --> 00:01:41.781
In the third act, he takes several hits from
automatic weapons, a shotgun blast to the

00:01:41.781 --> 00:01:45.990
chest, and even high-caliber rounds from hostile
snipers to almost no effect.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:49.710
In the middle of "The Batman," our hero finds
himself in the police precinct after being

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.929
rendered unconscious by the Riddler's explosive
execution of D.A.

00:01:52.929 --> 00:01:53.929
Gil Colson.

00:01:53.929 --> 00:01:58.020
This means that, aside from gunfire, he's
also taken the full force of a bomb explosion

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.020
up close.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:03.450
Then, when he escapes the entire police force,
he glides away from danger in his wingsuit.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.789
However, he doesn't quite nail the landing,
and instead, his parachute is caught on a

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:11.170
bridge, smashing the hero into a moving vehicle
and the concrete.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:16.250
While he does hobble away in pain, he recovers
rather quickly to continue his vigilante work,

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.750
which seems to indicate that he didn't suffer
too greatly.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:23.000
For all intents and purposes, this armor seems
a little too magical.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.210
The Riddler is a frightening foe, at least
in Matt Reeves' version of the character.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.670
Batman is known for maintaining a coterie
of supervillains who are mostly insane or

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:31.920
mentally unstable.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.530
The Joker typically might win in the "creep"
factor department, but in this version of

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.950
the Batman lore, the Riddler operates like
an absolute nightmare.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.170
If we didn't know any better, the opening
scene alone, where the Riddler stalks the

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:46.490
mayor before bludgeoning him to death, might
indicate that we're watching a slasher horror

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.490
film.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.940
Aside from the Riddler's murderous methods,
he seems to enjoy savoring his kills.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:55.090
He stands in the shadows for quite some time
watching the mayor pacing only a few feet

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:58.210
from him while watching the news coverage
of his campaign for reelection.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.570
Later, the Riddler provides the media with
footage of him killing the current police

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.870
commissioner using a Jigsaw-like trap in which
rats are guided through a maze and ultimately

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.990
forced to attack the commissioner's face to
escape.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:12.210
It's a dark and macabre setting for a villain
who's completely unhinged and ready to do

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.670
anything to achieve his goals.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.440
The horror elements of this film are jarring
and unforgettable.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:21.020
Paul Dano's performance of the character continues
to deliver terror even after he is unmasked

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.530
and sitting behind hardened glass opposite
of Batman.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.620
His erratic yelling and pervasive tics all
tell a story.

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:35.210
We know that the Riddler had a horrible childhood,
and it clearly made him a horrible man.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.210
"You came.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.210
I've been trying to reach you."

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.750
One of the film's most intense moments is
when Batman gives chase to the Penguin, believing

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.940
him to be the rat the Riddler is leading him
to.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.060
The monstrous Batmobile roars onto the scene
letting the Penguin know there's no escape.

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.580
Despite the reality of an angry Batman burning
rubber in a jacked hot-rod with a steel frame,

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:54.880
the Penguin still attempts to shake his pursuer
the only way he knows how — by driving head-first

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.190
into oncoming traffic.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:04:00.110
Eventually, the Penguin causes a massive pile-up,
leading to an explosion.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:03.760
It briefly seems as though the Penguin has
either lost the Batman or killed him.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.280
As he speeds away, however, the Batmobile
comes streaking out of the fire and pummels

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.940
the Penguin's vehicle, sending him tumbling
across the interstate.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:14.440
Batman and Jim Gordon then interrogate the
Penguin before abandoning him for another

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.440
lead.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.930
While the massive destruction on the interstate
is pulse-pounding, it's quickly forgotten

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:20.199
by the film's characters.

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:24.289
Sure, Batman didn't cause the destruction,
and yes, this film is focused on a Batman

00:04:24.289 --> 00:04:26.280
fighting out of hate, not hope.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.999
As such, it makes sense that the Penguin would
be all he is concerned about instead of helping

00:04:29.999 --> 00:04:31.580
the innocents among the wreckage.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:35.810
However, the Penguin receives no consequences
for those actions, and squeaky-clean police

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:38.560
lieutenant Jim Gordon seems undeterred by
it as well.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.550
The pile-up was simply an explosive action
sequence without any real effect.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:45.689
It's also a bit of a head-scratcher.

00:04:45.689 --> 00:04:47.819
"I got you!"

00:04:47.819 --> 00:04:51.430
"The Batman" is an engaging, character-heavy
story.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:55.129
The film is anchored by a talented cast who
capably take on their roles.

00:04:55.129 --> 00:04:59.880
Oz Cobblepot, the future Penguin, is one character
that is brilliantly realized from head to

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:00.880
toe.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:04.170
Make-up and prosthetics ensure that we never
recognize Colin Farrell, even if we know he

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.169
is somewhere underneath that rough exterior.

00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:10.360
Farrell perfects his performance by depicting
a wildly believable and captivating mobster

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:12.949
who cares very little about anyone but himself.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:15.449
Batman confronts the Penguin on two separate
occasions.

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:19.389
The first time is more of an amicable meeting
as Batman attempts to find any information

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:23.580
linking the mayor to organized crime and the
cesspool of individuals that occupy the Iceberg

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.710
Lounge.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.820
Penguin sarcastically humors the Dark Knight.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.630
Later, Batman pursues the Penguin after learning
that he may have been the man who ratted on

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:33.029
Sal Maroni's illicit business operations.

00:05:33.029 --> 00:05:37.290
However, the Penguin isn't the man the Caped
Crusader is looking for.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.749
In the interrogation, the Penguin establishes
himself as a bullish yet witty individual

00:05:40.749 --> 00:05:42.680
who will do anything to survive.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:47.199
After all, the Penguin is a survivor and even
outlasted Carmine Falcone and will soon secure

00:05:47.199 --> 00:05:50.289
power for himself — there's no doubt about
that.

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:54.150
While he doesn't get a ton of screen time,
the Penguin is absolutely magnetic every time

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:56.090
he appears on camera.

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.090
Everyone knows Bruce Wayne’s tragic backstory.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:02.949
We also know that the death of his parents
leads Alfred to become Bruce's surrogate family.

00:06:02.949 --> 00:06:06.669
Typically positioned as a faithful servant
of the Wayne family, Alfred stands by Bruce

00:06:06.669 --> 00:06:07.870
through thick and thin.

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:11.590
“The Batman” even establishes that he
likely taught Bruce how to fight, which means

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.219
that Alfred is one tough cookie.

00:06:13.219 --> 00:06:17.010
He even hints at the idea that he may have
been more of a bodyguard to the Waynes than

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:20.759
just a simple servant, when he tells Bruce
that he was supposed to protect Thomas and

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:21.759
Martha.

00:06:21.759 --> 00:06:24.800
Whatever the case may be, there's certainly
a history between the two that's begging to

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:25.800
be explored.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:29.300
However, the film doesn't really touch on
the relationship between the two in any meaningful

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.300
way.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.259
Sure, Alfred helps Bruce crack Riddler's ciphers.

00:06:32.259 --> 00:06:36.469
He even takes the full force of a bomb for
Bruce and is hospitalized as a result.

00:06:36.469 --> 00:06:40.379
But when Bruce finally tells Alfred that he
fears losing someone he cares about, it doesn't

00:06:40.379 --> 00:06:44.659
exactly feel earned, given the lack of interaction
between the two.

00:06:44.659 --> 00:06:48.840
Despite Batman's penchant for working alone,
he needs allies beyond Alfred.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:53.199
Selina Kyle fills that role in "The Batman,"
and Zoë Kravitz completely slays in her performance

00:06:53.199 --> 00:06:54.199
as the famous cat-burglar.

00:06:54.199 --> 00:06:56.719
"Maybe we're not so different.

00:06:56.719 --> 00:06:59.319
Who are you under there?"

00:06:59.319 --> 00:07:03.969
As a character, she's far more multi-dimensional
than the always angry Batman is at the start

00:07:03.969 --> 00:07:04.979
of the film.

00:07:04.979 --> 00:07:08.889
Selina is compassionate, fiercely loyal to
her friends, and extremely deadly in the right

00:07:08.889 --> 00:07:09.889
situations.

00:07:09.889 --> 00:07:13.499
When Batman first catches her off guard while
breaking into a safe, she trades blows with

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:16.210
the Dark Knight, and the two have magnetic
chemistry right away.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:20.310
When the big revelation drops that Carmine
Falcone is Selina's father and that she's

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:23.400
gunning for him, a new side to the character
is unveiled.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:27.259
Selina doesn't play around, and regardless
of any blood relation, messing with her friends

00:07:27.259 --> 00:07:28.690
might earn you a bullet.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:33.129
Catwoman has always been a conflicted figure
who often balances her thievery with her respect

00:07:33.129 --> 00:07:34.199
for Batman.

00:07:34.199 --> 00:07:38.039
Kravitz's portrayal is, possibly, the most
accurate live-action depiction of the character

00:07:38.039 --> 00:07:39.729
yet.

00:07:39.729 --> 00:07:43.070
Batman is known for his famous Batcave, where
all the toys and equipment reside.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:46.610
"The Batman" does away with the idea of the
cave being below Wayne Manor.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:50.419
Instead, Bruce Wayne lives in a skyscraper,
and his Batcave appears to be an abandoned

00:07:50.419 --> 00:07:51.449
subway station.

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:54.349
Creative choices abound in the film, and most
of them are hits.

00:07:54.349 --> 00:07:58.229
However, the lack of a substantial Batcave,
while a nitpick, might weigh heavily on the

00:07:58.229 --> 00:07:59.509
hearts of Bat-fans.

00:07:59.509 --> 00:08:03.699
The space Batman uses is in keeping with a
minimalist vibe one might get from the early

00:08:03.699 --> 00:08:04.949
days of Batman's career.

00:08:04.949 --> 00:08:08.080
However, it also feels largely unimpressive
and uninspired.

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:11.869
The Batcave is an iconic piece of Batman's
history that ultimately deserves a certain

00:08:11.869 --> 00:08:13.460
reverence in its depiction.

00:08:13.460 --> 00:08:17.129
Hopefully, Bruce Wayne will expand operations
in the follow-up film and take his work to

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.759
a more suitable home base.

00:08:18.759 --> 00:08:23.750
"The Batman" is teeming with the crooks, thieves,
and killers that populate the seedier side

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:24.770
of Gotham City.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:28.719
The film drops hints and clues about a larger
world of Batman lore and characters that the

00:08:28.719 --> 00:08:30.249
sequels can flesh out.

00:08:30.249 --> 00:08:33.650
Throughout the Riddler's campaign for justice,
he seeks to assassinate the character of the

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:37.139
city's leadership by exposing their most heinous
truths to the public.

00:08:37.139 --> 00:08:40.970
During some of his ramblings that hit the
airwaves, he discusses important figureheads

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.190
in Gotham City like the Arkham family.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:47.430
One of his newspaper clippings even references
Edward Elliot, another popular Gothamite who

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:49.050
helped modernize the city.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:53.050
His descendent, Tommy Elliot, even becomes
the villainous Hush in the comics.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:57.490
Later, Batman uses a venom-like substance
to receive a boost of unbridled energy, which

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:00.190
indicates that Bane might be in Batman's future.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:04.430
Mentions of Blackgate Prison, Arkham State
Hospital, and even Bludhaven are woven in

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:05.570
the film's dialogue.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:08.019
These are all locales iconic to Batman lore.

00:09:08.019 --> 00:09:11.180
Audiences even get a glimpse of Arkham with
the Riddler in his cell.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:16.139
The film even teases a popular Batman villain
who cackles at the Riddler's comeback plans.

00:09:16.139 --> 00:09:19.310
There's plenty happening within the world
of "The Batman," making it one of the film's

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:22.110
best qualities for Bat-fans.

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:25.860
In the film's opening moments, Batman saves
a man from a ruthless beating at the hands

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:26.860
of a gang.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.670
Clearly, his goal wasn't to save the man but
to punish the wicked.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:33.899
After he frightens the goons away, the innocent
man is afraid of Batman and begs the vigilante

00:09:33.899 --> 00:09:35.000
not to hurt him.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.250
He doesn't, but neither does he offer any
message of comfort.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:42.709
Later in the film, Batman ignores a mass pile-up
and explosion on the freeway, which likely

00:09:42.709 --> 00:09:45.370
led to some casualties, in order to catch
Oz.

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:49.240
When Selina asks for his help finding a friend
who is clearly in danger, Batman cares more

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.620
about retrieving intel than the innocent whose
life is on the line.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:56.959
He's even icy cold toward Alfred and calls
him a liar after Alfred wakes up at the hospital.

00:09:56.959 --> 00:10:00.750
The ending of the film marks a welcome change
in the character as he focuses on providing

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.660
hope to the good citizens of Gotham.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.770
However, it's still hard to witness our hero
so enthralled in his quest for vengeance that

00:10:06.770 --> 00:10:10.769
he forgets what it's like to be human and
ignores the plight of others in distress.

